n  \nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n7 + 2 = 9 (units place)\n6 + 4 = 10 (tens place, so write down 0 and carry over 1)\n9 + 0 + 1 (carry-over) = 10 (hundreds place, so write down 0 and carry over 1)\nBut wait, there are no more digits to add, so the carried-over 1 becomes the thousands place.\n\nWait, that would make it 1009? Let me check that again.\n\nWait, 967 + 42:\n\n967 + 40 = 1007\n\nThen 1007 + 2 = 1009. Yes, that's correct. Wait, but let me verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, breaking down the numbers:\n\n967 can be thought of as 900 + 60 + 7\n\n42 is 40 + 2\n\nAdding them together:\n\n900 + (60 + 40) + (7 + 2) = 900 + 100 + 9 = 1009.\n\nYes, that's the same result. So s = 1009. Hmm, but wait, when I added the tens place earlier, I had 6 + 4 = 10, so that's 0 with a carry-over of 1 to the hundreds place. Then the hundreds place is 9 + 0 + 1 = 10, so that's 0 with a carry-over of 1 to the thousands place. Hence, 1 in thousands, 0 in hundreds, 0 in tens, 9 in units: 1009. That seems right.\n\nBut just to be absolutely sure, let me use another approach. Let me subtract 42 from 1009 and see if I get 967.\n\n1009 - 42 = ?\n\n1009 - 40 = 969\n\n969 - 2 = 967\n\nYes, that's correct. So the addition was done properly. Therefore, s is indeed 1009.\n\nWait a second, but I want to make sure that there isn't a simpler way I might have overlooked. Sometimes with arithmetic, it's easy to make a mistake in carrying over numbers. Let me try adding 967 and 42 step by step again.\n\nStarting with 967, if I add 10, that's 977. Adding another 10 is 987. Then another 10 is 997. Then another 10 is 1007. So that's 40 added, which brings us to 1007. Then add the remaining 2 to get 1009. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, using number line: 967 + 42. Start at 967, jump 30 to reach 997, then jump 12 more: 997 + 10 = 1007, then +2 = 1009. All methods confirm that 967 + 42 = 1009.\n\nTherefore, the value of s is 1009. I think that's solid. No mistakes in the calculations here. All cross-checks add up. So I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n\n\n\nThe value of \\( s \\) is calculated by adding the given values of \\( e \\) and 42:\n\n\\[\ns = e + 42 = 967 + 42 = 1009\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. Start with \\( e = 967 \\).\n2. Add 42 to \\( e \\):  \n   \\[\n   967 + 42 = 1009\n   \\]\n3. Verify using column addition:  \n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n    967 \\\\\n   +\\,42 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   1009 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - Units place: \\( 7 + 2 = 9 \\)  \n   - Tens place: \\( 6 + 4 = 10 \\) (write 0, carry over 1)  \n   - Hundreds place: \\( 9 + 0 + 1 = 10 \\) (write 0, carry over 1)  \n   - Thousands place: \\( 1 \\)\n\n**Answer:**  \n\\( s = \\boxed{1009} \\)"}
