All right, I think that's more than enough verification. The answer is 529. I can't see any mistakes in my calculations, and all different methods of subtracting give me the same result. So p must be 529.\n\n\n\nThe value of \\( p \\) is calculated by subtracting 63 from 592:\n\n\\[\np = l - 63 = 592 - 63\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down step-by-step:\n1. Subtract the ones place: \\( 2 - 3 \\) requires borrowing, resulting in \\( 12 - 3 = 9 \\).\n2. Subtract the tens place: After borrowing, \\( 8 - 6 = 2 \\).\n3. The hundreds place remains \\( 5 \\).\n\nCombining these, we get:\n\n\\[\np = 529\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** 529"}
