 my previous result. \n\nHmm, just to be thorough, maybe I can add 21 to 433 to see if I get back to 454. 433 plus 20 is 453, plus 1 is 454. Perfect, that confirms that the subtraction was done correctly. \n\nSo, after substituting r with 454 in the expression for c, we correctly calculate c as 433. I don't see any complications here. The operations are straightforward, and there's no ambiguity in the problem statement. The variables are clearly defined, and the operations are basic arithmetic. \n\nTherefore, I can confidently conclude that the value of c is 433.\n\n\n\nThe value of \\( c \\) is calculated as follows:\n\nGiven:\n\\[\nr = 454\n\\]\n\\[\nc = r - 21\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( r \\) with 454:\n\\[\nc = 454 - 21\n\\]\n\nPerform the subtraction:\n\\[\n454 - 21 = 433\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{433}\\)"}
