add 22 \u2192 total change -90 +22 = -68  \nx: subtract 48 \u2192 total change -68 -48 = -116  \nq: add 21 \u2192 total change -116 +21 = -95  \ns: add 86 \u2192 total change -95 +86 = -9  \ng: subtract 67 \u2192 total change -9 -67 = -76  \nf: add 89 \u2192 total change -76 +89 = +13  \n\nTherefore, f = o +13 = 923 +13 =936. Perfect, this method also confirms the answer. So no matter which method I use\u2014step-by-step computation, substitution, or cumulative change\u2014the result is 936. I think that solidifies the answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm pretty confident that f is 936.\n\n\n\nThe value of \\( f \\) is calculated step-by-step as follows:\n\n1. \\( o = 923 \\)\n2. \\( r = o - 90 = 923 - 90 = 833 \\)\n3. \\( z = r + 22 = 833 + 22 = 855 \\)\n4. \\( x = z - 48 = 855 - 48 = 807 \\)\n5. \\( q = x + 21 = 807 + 21 = 828 \\)\n6. \\( s = q + 86 = 828 + 86 = 914 \\)\n7. \\( g = s - 67 = 914 - 67 = 847 \\)\n8. \\( f = g + 89 = 847 + 89 = 936 \\)\n\nAlternatively, summing the cumulative changes from \\( o \\) to \\( f \\):  \nTotal change = \\(-90 + 22 - 48 + 21 + 86 - 67 + 89 = +13\\)  \nThus, \\( f = o + 13 = 923 + 13 = 936 \\).\n\n\\(\\boxed{936}\\)"}
