959. So j = 959. Checking: 977 - 18. 900 - 0 = 900, 70 - 10 = 60, 7 - 8. Hmm, maybe another way: 977 - 20 = 957, but since we only need to subtract 18, add back 2: 957 + 2 = 959. Correct.\n\n7. **p = j + 39**  \n   j is 959. Adding 39. Let's see, 959 + 30 = 989, then +9 more is 998. So p = 998. Let me check: 959 + 39. 900 + 30 = 930, 50 + 9 = 59, 9 + 0 = 9. Wait, maybe that's not the right way. Alternatively, 959 + 40 = 999, subtract 1: 999 -1 = 998. Yes, that works. So p = 998.\n\n8. **g = p + 98**  \n   Finally, p is 998. Adding 98. Let's compute 998 + 100 = 1098, then subtract 2: 1098 - 2 = 1096. So g = 1096. Checking: 998 + 98. 900 + 90 = 990, 90 + 8 = 98, 8 + 8 = 16. Wait, maybe that's not the right breakdown. Alternatively, 998 + 98 = (998 + 2) + 96 = 1000 + 96 = 1096. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo, following each step carefully and verifying each calculation, I arrive at g being 1096. Let me just go through all the steps again quickly to ensure I didn't make any mistakes:\n\n- f = 911  \n- n = 911 - 75 = 836  \n- w = 836 + 74 = 910  \n- y = 910 + 10 = 920  \n- u = 920 + 57 = 977  \n- j = 977 - 18 = 959  \n- p = 959 + 39 = 998  \n- g = 998 + 98 = 1096  \n\nEach step seems to check out. Maybe I can see if there's a pattern or a shortcut, but since each variable depends on the previous one, I think computing step by step is necessary. Alternatively, maybe substitute all the equations into one expression for g.\n\nLet's try that:\n\nStarting with f = 911,\n\nn = f - 75  \nw = n + 74 = (f - 75) + 74 = f - 1  \ny = w + 10 = (f - 1) + 10 = f + 9  \nu = y + 57 = (f + 9) + 57 = f + 66  \nj = u - 18 = (f + 66) - 18 = f + 48  \np = j + 39 = (f + 48) + 39 = f + 87  \ng = p + 98 = (f + 87) + 98 = f + 185  \n\nOh! Wait, that's a much quicker way. If I substitute each equation into the next, I can express g in terms of f directly. Since f = 911, then g = 911 + 185 = 1096. That's the same result as before. So that's a good check. So substituting all the intermediate variables, we find that each operation cancels out or adds up. Let me verify the substitutions:\n\nStarting with n = f - 75  \nThen w = n + 74 = (f - 75) + 74 = f - 1  \ny = w + 10 = (f - 1) + 10 = f + 9  \nu = y + 57 = (f + 9) + 57 = f + 66  \nj = u - 18 = (f + 66) - 18 = f + 48  \np = j + 39 = (f + 48) + 39 = f + 87  \ng = p + 98 = (f + 87) + 98 = f + 185  \n\nYes, that's correct. Each step simplifies the expression in terms of f. So since f is 911, then g = 911 + 185. Let's compute that: 911 + 100 = 1011, 1011 + 85 = 1096. Yep, same answer.\n\nThis gives me more confidence that the answer is indeed 1096. It's always good to check the work in two different ways: once by computing each variable step by step, and another by substituting all the equations into a single expression. Both methods led to the same result, so I think that's solid.\n\nI don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Maybe another way to check is to reverse the operations. If g = 1096, then p = g - 98 = 1096 - 98 = 998. Then j = p - 39 = 998 - 39 = 959. Then u = j + 18 = 959 + 18 = 977. Then y = u - 57 = 977 - 57 = 920. Then w = y - 10 = 920 - 10 = 910. Then n = w - 74 = 910 - 74 = 836. Then f = n + 75 = 836 + 75 = 911. Which matches the original value of f. So reversing the steps also leads back to the original f, confirming that all the intermediate steps are consistent.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the value of g is 1096.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe value of \\( g \\) is \\boxed{1096}.\n\n\n\nGiven the assignments:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nf &= 911, \\\\\nn &= f - 75, \\\\\nw &= n + 74, \\\\\ny &= w + 10, \\\\\nu &= y + 57, \\\\\nj &= u - 18, \\\\\np &= j + 39, \\\\\ng &= p + 98.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( g \\).\n\nFirst, we substitute each variable step by step:\n\n1. \\( f = 911 \\)\n2. \\( n = f - 75 = 911 - 75 = 836 \\)\n3. \\( w = n + 74 = 836 + 74 = 910 \\)\n4. \\( y = w + 10 = 910 + 10 = 920 \\)\n5. \\( u = y + 57 = 920 + 57 = 977 \\)\n6. \\( j = u - 18 = 977 - 18 = 959 \\)\n7. \\( p = j + 39 = 959 + 39 = 998 \\)\n8. \\( g = p + 98 = 998 + 98 = 1096 \\)\n\nWe can also verify this by expressing \\( g \\) in terms of \\( f \\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nn &= f - 75, \\\\\nw &= (f - 75) + 74 = f - 1, \\\\\ny &= (f - 1) + 10 = f + 9, \\\\\nu &= (f + 9) + 57 = f + 66, \\\\\nj &= (f + 66) - 18 = f + 48, \\\\\np &= (f + 48) + 39 = f + 87, \\\\\ng &= (f + 87) + 98 = f + 185.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSince \\( f = 911 \\):\n\n\\[\ng = 911 + 185 = 1096\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( g \\) is \\(\\boxed{1096}\\)."}
