 is 448.\n\nMoving on, f is l minus 50. That would be 448 - 50. 448 minus 40 is 408, minus 10 more is 398. So f is 398.\n\nNext, j is f minus 64. So 398 - 64. Hmm, 398 minus 60 is 338, then minus 4 is 334. So j is 334.\n\nThen i is j plus 81. So 334 + 81. Let's break that down. 334 + 80 is 414, then +1 is 415. So i is 415.\n\nAfter that, g is i plus 40. So 415 + 40. That's straightforward: 415 + 40 is 455. Therefore, g is 455.\n\nThen z is g plus 13. 455 + 13. 455 + 10 is 465, plus 3 is 468. So z is 468.\n\nNext is v, which is z plus 51. So 468 + 51. Let's calculate that. 468 + 50 is 518, plus 1 is 519. Therefore, v is 519.\n\nThen n is v plus 27. 519 + 27. 519 + 20 is 539, plus 7 is 546. So n is 546.\n\nk is n minus 75. So 546 - 75. Hmm, 546 minus 70 is 476, then minus 5 is 471. So k is 471.\n\ns is k plus 67. 471 + 67. Let's see, 471 + 60 is 531, then +7 is 538. So s is 538.\n\nNext, m is s minus 77. So 538 - 77. 538 minus 70 is 468, minus 7 more is 461. Therefore, m is 461.\n\nThen w is m minus 85. 461 - 85. 461 minus 80 is 381, minus 5 is 376. So w is 376.\n\nFinally, t is w minus 56. 376 - 56. That's 376 - 50 = 326, then minus 6 is 320. So t should be 320.\n\nWait, let me check each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Starting from b=480:\n\nc = 480 -74 = 406 \u2714\ufe0f\n\ny=406-14=392 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nl=392+56=448 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nf=448-50=398 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nj=398-64=334 \u2714\ufe0f\n\ni=334+81=415 \u2714\ufe0f\n\ng=415+40=455 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nz=455+13=468 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nv=468+51=519 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nn=519+27=546 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nk=546-75=471 \u2714\ufe0f\n\ns=471+67=538 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nm=538-77=461 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nw=461-85=376 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nt=376-56=320 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHmm, seems all the steps check out. So t is 320. I think that's it. Let me just verify with another approach. Maybe substitute each variable into the next equation to see if it holds.\n\nStarting from t = w -56, and w = m -85, so t = (m -85) -56 = m -141. Then m = s -77, so t = (s -77) -141 = s -218. s = k +67, so t = (k +67) -218 = k -151. k = n -75, so t = (n -75) -151 = n -226. n = v +27, so t = (v +27) -226 = v -199. v = z +51, so t = (z +51) -199 = z -148. z = g +13, so t = (g +13) -148 = g -135. g = i +40, so t = (i +40) -135 = i -95. i = j +81, so t = (j +81) -95 = j -14. j = f -64, so t = (f -64) -14 = f -78. f = l -50, so t = (l -50) -78 = l -128. l = y +56, so t = (y +56) -128 = y -72. y = c -14, so t = (c -14) -72 = c -86. c = b -74, so t = (b -74) -86 = b -160. Since b is 480, t = 480 -160 = 320. Yep, same result. That confirms it. So t is definitely 320. I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe value of \\( t \\) is \\(\\boxed{320}\\).\n\n\n\nStarting with the given assignments, we calculate each subsequent variable step by step:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nb &= 480, \\\\\nc &= b - 74 = 480 - 74 = 406, \\\\\ny &= c - 14 = 406 - 14 = 392, \\\\\nl &= y + 56 = 392 + 56 = 448, \\\\\nf &= l - 50 = 448 - 50 = 398, \\\\\nj &= f - 64 = 398 - 64 = 334, \\\\\ni &= j + 81 = 334 + 81 = 415, \\\\\ng &= i + 40 = 415 + 40 = 455, \\\\\nz &= g + 13 = 455 + 13 = 468, \\\\\nv &= z + 51 = 468 + 51 = 519, \\\\\nn &= v + 27 = 519 + 27 = 546, \\\\\nk &= n - 75 = 546 - 75 = 471, \\\\\ns &= k + 67 = 471 + 67 = 538, \\\\\nm &= s - 77 = 538 - 77 = 461, \\\\\nw &= m - 85 = 461 - 85 = 376, \\\\\nt &= w - 56 = 376 - 56 = 320.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( t \\) is \\(\\boxed{320}\\)."}
