+ 66\np = l - 78\n\nOkay, so p is the last one, and each variable is built from the one before. Let's compute each one step by step. Maybe I can do this sequentially, substituting each value as we go along.\n\nStarting with i = 130. Then j is i minus 26. So j = 130 - 26. Let me calculate that: 130 minus 20 is 110, then minus 6 is 104. So j = 104.\n\nNext is v = j + 45. Since j is 104, v = 104 + 45. Let's see, 100 + 45 is 145, plus 4 is 149. So v = 149.\n\nThen x = v + 20. v is 149, so x = 149 + 20. That's 169. So x = 169.\n\nNext, f = x - 67. x is 169, so 169 - 67. Let's subtract 60 from 169, which is 109, then subtract 7 more: 102. So f = 102.\n\nThen u = f - 27. f is 102, so 102 - 27. Hmm, 102 - 20 is 82, then minus 7 is 75. So u = 75.\n\nNext up is h = u - 55. u is 75, so 75 - 55. That's straightforward: 20. So h = 20.\n\nThen e = h + 72. h is 20, so 20 + 72 = 92. Therefore, e = 92.\n\nMoving on, t = e - 95. e is 92, so 92 - 95. Wait, that's going to be a negative number. 92 minus 95 is -3. So t = -3.\n\nNext, w = t - 65. t is -3, so -3 - 65. That's -68. So w = -68.\n\nThen s = w - 93. w is -68, so -68 - 93. Let's see, that's like -(68 + 93). 68 + 90 is 158, plus 3 is 161. So s = -161.\n\nNext variable is b = s + 54. s is -161, so -161 + 54. Hmm, that's like -(161 - 54). 161 - 50 is 111, minus 4 is 107. So -107. Therefore, b = -107.\n\nThen z = b - 98. b is -107, so -107 - 98. Again, combining the negatives: - (107 + 98) = -205. So z = -205.\n\nNext is d = z - 80. z is -205, so -205 - 80 = -285. Therefore, d = -285.\n\nThen l = d + 66. d is -285, so -285 + 66. Let's subtract 66 from 285 first. 285 - 60 = 225, minus 6 = 219. So since it's -285 + 66, that's -219. Wait, no. Wait: -285 + 66 is the same as -(285 - 66). Let me compute 285 - 66. 285 - 60 is 225, then minus 6 is 219. So -219. Therefore, l = -219.\n\nFinally, p = l - 78. l is -219, so -219 - 78. That's like -(219 + 78). Let's compute 219 + 70 = 289, then +8 = 297. So p = -297.\n\nWait, let me check my steps again to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. Sometimes when dealing with negatives, it's easy to slip up.\n\nStarting from i = 130:\n\ni = 130  \nj = 130 - 26 = 104 \u2714\ufe0f  \nv = 104 + 45 = 149 \u2714\ufe0f  \nx = 149 + 20 = 169 \u2714\ufe0f  \nf = 169 - 67 = 102 \u2714\ufe0f  \nu = 102 - 27 = 75 \u2714\ufe0f  \nh = 75 - 55 = 20 \u2714\ufe0f  \ne = 20 + 72 = 92 \u2714\ufe0f  \nt = 92 - 95 = -3 \u2714\ufe0f  \nw = -3 - 65 = -68 \u2714\ufe0f  \ns = -68 - 93 = -161 \u2714\ufe0f  \nb = -161 + 54 = -107 \u2714\ufe0f  \nz = -107 - 98 = -205 \u2714\ufe0f  \nd = -205 - 80 = -285 \u2714\ufe0f  \nl = -285 + 66 = -219 \u2714\ufe0f  \np = -219 - 78 = -297 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHmm, seems like all steps check out. Each time, the calculation follows correctly. So even though there are some negative numbers involved, each step is correctly computed. Therefore, p is indeed -297.\n\nBut let me just cross-verify the last few steps again because the numbers get quite large in the negative.\n\nStarting from z = -205:\n\nd = z - 80 = -205 -80 = -285. Yes, because -205 minus 80 is -285.  \nl = d + 66 = -285 + 66. Let's compute this: if you have -285 and add 60, you get -225, then add 6 more: -219. Correct.  \np = l -78 = -219 -78. Breaking it down: -219 -70 is -289, then -8 more is -297. Yep, that's right.\n\nSo, all steps are correct. Therefore, the final value of p is -297.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe value of \\( p \\) is \\boxed{-297}.\n\n\n\nStarting with the given assignments:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\ni &= 130 \\\\\nj &= i - 26 = 130 - 26 = 104 \\\\\nv &= j + 45 = 104 + 45 = 149 \\\\\nx &= v + 20 = 149 + 20 = 169 \\\\\nf &= x - 67 = 169 - 67 = 102 \\\\\nu &= f - 27 = 102 - 27 = 75 \\\\\nh &= u - 55 = 75 - 55 = 20 \\\\\ne &= h + 72 = 20 + 72 = 92 \\\\\nt &= e - 95 = 92 - 95 = -3 \\\\\nw &= t - 65 = -3 - 65 = -68 \\\\\ns &= w - 93 = -68 - 93 = -161 \\\\\nb &= s + 54 = -161 + 54 = -107 \\\\\nz &= b - 98 = -107 - 98 = -205 \\\\\nd &= z - 80 = -205 - 80 = -285 \\\\\nl &= d + 66 = -285 + 66 = -219 \\\\\np &= l - 78 = -219 - 78 = -297 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThe value of \\( p \\) is \\(\\boxed{-297}\\)."}
