. Wait, 305 + 55. Let me check again. 300 + 50 is 350, 5 + 5 is 10, so total 360. Yeah, b = 360.\n\nThen f = b - 38. 360 minus 38. 360 - 30 is 330, minus 8 is 322. So f = 322.\n\nh = f - 75. 322 minus 75. Hmm, 322 - 70 is 252, minus 5 is 247. So h = 247.\n\ny = h - 39. 247 - 39. Let's subtract 40 first, which would be 207, but since it's 39, add 1 back. So 207 + 1 = 208. So y = 208.\n\nw = y - 63. 208 - 63. 200 - 60 is 140, 8 - 3 is 5, so total 145. Wait, 208 - 60 is 148, then minus 3 more is 145. Yeah, so w = 145.\n\ne = w - 20. 145 - 20 = 125. So e = 125.\n\nl = e - 82. 125 - 82. Let me do 125 - 80 = 45, then minus 2 is 43. So l = 43.\n\nu = l - 66. 43 - 66. Hmm, that's negative. 43 - 60 is -17, minus 6 more is -23. So u = -23.\n\ns = u - 98. -23 - 98. That's like -(23 + 98) = -121. So s = -121.\n\nv = s - 61. -121 - 61 = -182. So v = -182.\n\np = v + 72. -182 + 72. Let's see, 72 - 182. 182 - 72 is 110, so it's -110. Wait, no. If you have -182 + 72, that's like subtracting 72 from 182 but keeping the sign. Wait, maybe better to think as -182 + 70 is -112, plus 2 is -110. So p = -110.\n\nx = p + 35. -110 + 35. That's -75. Because 110 - 35 is 75, so negative. So x = -75.\n\nn = x + 78. So -75 + 78. That's 3. Because 78 - 75 = 3. So n = 3.\n\nWait, let me check all these steps again to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. Starting from g=387:\n\n1. a = 387 - 43 = 344 \u2714\ufe0f\n2. q = 344 - 39 = 305 \u2714\ufe0f\n3. b = 305 + 55 = 360 \u2714\ufe0f\n4. f = 360 - 38 = 322 \u2714\ufe0f\n5. h = 322 - 75 = 247 \u2714\ufe0f\n6. y = 247 - 39 = 208 \u2714\ufe0f\n7. w = 208 - 63 = 145 \u2714\ufe0f\n8. e = 145 - 20 = 125 \u2714\ufe0f\n9. l = 125 - 82 = 43 \u2714\ufe0f\n10. u = 43 - 66 = -23 \u2714\ufe0f\n11. s = -23 - 98 = -121 \u2714\ufe0f\n12. v = -121 - 61 = -182 \u2714\ufe0f\n13. p = -182 + 72 = -110 \u2714\ufe0f\n14. x = -110 + 35 = -75 \u2714\ufe0f\n15. n = -75 + 78 = 3 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nSeems like all the steps check out. So the final value of n is 3.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe value of \\( n \\) is \\boxed{3}.\n\n\n\nStarting with the given assignments, we compute each variable step by step:\n\n1. \\( g = 387 \\)\n2. \\( a = g - 43 = 387 - 43 = 344 \\)\n3. \\( q = a - 39 = 344 - 39 = 305 \\)\n4. \\( b = q + 55 = 305 + 55 = 360 \\)\n5. \\( f = b - 38 = 360 - 38 = 322 \\)\n6. \\( h = f - 75 = 322 - 75 = 247 \\)\n7. \\( y = h - 39 = 247 - 39 = 208 \\)\n8. \\( w = y - 63 = 208 - 63 = 145 \\)\n9. \\( e = w - 20 = 145 - 20 = 125 \\)\n10. \\( l = e - 82 = 125 - 82 = 43 \\)\n11. \\( u = l - 66 = 43 - 66 = -23 \\)\n12. \\( s = u - 98 = -23 - 98 = -121 \\)\n13. \\( v = s - 61 = -121 - 61 = -182 \\)\n14. \\( p = v + 72 = -182 + 72 = -110 \\)\n15. \\( x = p + 35 = -110 + 35 = -75 \\)\n16. \\( n = x + 78 = -75 + 78 = 3 \\)\n\nThe value of \\( n \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\)."}
