nThen, c = j + 20. Plugging in j's value: 313 + 20. That would be 333. So c = 333.\n\nNext is a = c - 63. Substituting c: 333 - 63. Let me do the subtraction: 333 - 60 is 273, then minus 3 more is 270. So a = 270.\n\nMoving on, s = a + 75. With a being 270, that's 270 + 75. Adding those together: 270 + 70 is 340, plus 5 is 345. So s = 345.\n\nThen z = s - 55. So 345 - 55. Hmm, 345 - 50 is 295, then minus 5 is 290. So z = 290.\n\nNext up is n = z + 36. Using z's value: 290 + 36. Let me add that: 290 + 30 is 320, plus 6 is 326. So n = 326.\n\nWait, that's interesting. n is 326, which is the same as y. Maybe that's a coincidence or maybe it loops back? Let's continue.\n\nm = n + 85. Since n is 326, m = 326 + 85. Let's compute that: 326 + 80 is 406, plus 5 is 411. So m = 411.\n\nThen q = m - 94. Substituting m: 411 - 94. Hmm, 411 - 90 is 321, then subtract 4 more: 321 - 4 = 317. So q = 317.\n\nNext, l = q + 89. So 317 + 89. Let's add: 317 + 80 is 397, plus 9 is 406. So l = 406.\n\nThen e = l + 56. That's 406 + 56. Adding step by step: 406 + 50 is 456, plus 6 is 462. So e = 462.\n\nNext is r = e - 83. Substituting e: 462 - 83. Let me subtract: 462 - 80 is 382, minus 3 more is 379. So r = 379.\n\nThen d = r - 94. So 379 - 94. Subtract 90 first: 379 - 90 is 289, then subtract 4: 289 - 4 = 285. Therefore, d = 285.\n\np = d - 83. So 285 - 83. Let's compute: 285 - 80 is 205, minus 3 is 202. So p = 202.\n\nh = p + 70. Substituting p: 202 + 70. That's straightforward: 202 + 70 = 272. So h = 272.\n\nFinally, w = h + 71. With h being 272, that's 272 + 71. Let me add: 272 + 70 is 342, plus 1 is 343. Therefore, w = 343.\n\nLet me double-check each step to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors.\n\nStarting from y = 326.\n\nj = 326 - 13 = 313 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nc = 313 + 20 = 333 \u2714\ufe0f\n\na = 333 - 63 = 270 \u2714\ufe0f\n\ns = 270 + 75 = 345 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nz = 345 - 55 = 290 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nn = 290 + 36 = 326 \u2714\ufe0f (same as y, interesting)\n\nm = 326 + 85 = 411 \u