0, l = 310 - 52. Hmm, 310 minus 50 is 260, then minus 2 more is 258. So l = 258.\n\nThen t = l - 35. Substituting l's value, t = 258 - 35. Let's see, 258 minus 30 is 228, minus 5 more is 223. So t = 223.\n\nMoving on to w = t - 31. So that's 223 - 31. Let me subtract 30 from 223, which is 193, then minus 1 more is 192. So w = 192.\n\nNext up is j = w + 65. With w being 192, j = 192 + 65. Adding 200 would be 257, but since it's 192 + 65, that's 192 + 60 = 252, plus 5 is 257. So j = 257.\n\nThen y = j - 96. Substituting j, y = 257 - 96. Let me subtract 100 from 257, which is 157, but since I subtracted 4 more than needed, I need to add back 4. So 157 + 4 = 161. Therefore, y = 161.\n\nNow q = y + 79. So q = 161 + 79. Let's do 161 + 70 = 231, then +9 = 240. So q = 240.\n\nNext variable is x = q - 48. So x = 240 - 48. Subtracting 40 from 240 is 200, then minus 8 more is 192. So x = 192.\n\nThen m = x - 75. Substituting x, m = 192 - 75. Let's see, 192 - 70 = 122, then minus 5 more is 117. So m = 117.\n\nMoving on to n = m + 62. So n = 117 + 62. 100 + 60 = 160, 17 + 2 = 19, so total is 160 + 19 = 179. Hence, n = 179.\n\nThen a = n - 76. So a = 179 - 76. Let's subtract 70 from 179, which is 109, then subtract 6 more: 109 - 6 = 103. So a = 103.\n\nNext, o = a + 49. That's 103 + 49. 100 + 40 = 140, 3 + 9 = 12, so 140 + 12 = 152. Therefore, o = 152.\n\nThen b = o - 85. So b = 152 - 85. Subtracting 80 from 152 gives 72, then subtract 5 more: 72 - 5 = 67. So b = 67.\n\nNow h = b - 60. Substituting b, h = 67 - 60. That's straightforward: 67 - 60 = 7. So h = 7.\n\nFinally, k = h + 57. With h being 7, k = 7 + 57. 7 + 50 is 57, plus 7 more is 64. So k = 64.\n\nLet me just quickly check each step again to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors. Starting from r = 330:\n\n- c = 330 -20 = 310 \u2714\ufe0f\n- l = 310 -52 = 258 \u2714\ufe0f\n- t = 258 -35 = 223 \u2714\ufe0f\n- w = 223 -31 = 192 \u2714\ufe0f\n- j = 192 +65 = 257 \u2714\ufe0f\n- y = 257 -96 = 161 \u2714\ufe0f\n- q = 161 +79 = 240 \u2714\ufe0f\n- x = 240 -48 = 192 \u2714\ufe0f\n- m = 192 -75 = 117 \u2714\ufe0f\n- n = 117 +62 = 179 \u2714\ufe0f\n- a = 179 -76 = 103 \u2714\ufe0f\n- o = 103 +49 = 152 \u2714\ufe0f\n- b = 152 -85 = 67 \u2714\ufe0f\n- h = 67 -60 = 7 \u2714\ufe0f\n- k = 7 +57 = 64 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nAll the steps check out. Each calculation seems correct. So the final value of k is 64.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe value of \\( k \\) is \\boxed{64}.\n\n\n\nStarting with the given assignments:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nr &= 330 \\\\\nc &= r - 20 = 330 - 20 = 310 \\\\\nl &= c - 52 = 310 - 52 = 258 \\\\\nt &= l - 35 = 258 - 35 = 223 \\\\\nw &= t - 31 = 223 - 31 = 192 \\\\\nj &= w + 65 = 192 + 65 = 257 \\\\\ny &= j - 96 = 257 - 96 = 161 \\\\\nq &= y + 79 = 161 + 79 = 240 \\\\\nx &= q - 48 = 240 - 48 = 192 \\\\\nm &= x - 75 = 192 - 75 = 117 \\\\\nn &= m + 62 = 117 + 62 = 179 \\\\\na &= n - 76 = 179 - 76 = 103 \\\\\no &= a + 49 = 103 + 49 = 152 \\\\\nb &= o - 85 = 152 - 85 = 67 \\\\\nh &= b - 60 = 67 - 60 = 7 \\\\\nk &= h + 57 = 7 + 57 = 64 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThe value of \\( k \\) is \\(\\boxed{64}\\)."}
