676, 1678], [1822, 1824], [2742, 2744], [2755, 2757], [2780, 2782], [2784, 2786], [3519, 3521], [3529, 3531], [4805, 4807], [4828, 4830]], "ambiguous": false}, {"name": "cx", "value": "48", "written": true, "spans": [[2810, 2812], [2823, 2825], [2848, 2850], [2852, 2854], [3535, 3537], [3545, 3547], [4838, 4840], [4861, 4863]], "ambiguous": false}, {"name": "dw", "value": "30", "written": true, "spans": [[1025, 1027], [1108, 1110], [1191, 1193], [1264, 1266], [2448, 2450], [2878, 2880], [2891, 2893], [3551, 3553], [3639, 3641], [3687, 3689], [4871, 4873], [4926, 4928]], "ambiguous": false}], "externalization_fraction": 1.0, "n_clean": 30}, "trace": "Okay, let me try to figure out the value of dw step by step. There are a bunch of variables here, each assigned a value based on the previous ones. I need to go through each assignment one by one, making sure I don't make any mistakes along the way. Let's start from the beginning.\n\nFirst, the problem gives bs = 524. That's straightforward. Then:\n\num = bs + 22. So um would be 524 + 22. Let me calculate that. 524 + 20 is 544, then +2 more is 546. So um is 546.\n\nNext, et = um - 60. Since um is 546, subtracting 60 gives 546 - 60. Let's do that. 546 - 50 is 496, then minus 10 more is 486. So et is 486.\n\nThen ud = et - 94. et is 486. 486 - 94. Hmm, 486 - 90 is 396, then subtract 4 more: 396 - 4 = 392. So ud is 392.\n\nhw = ud - 83. ud is 392. 392 - 80 is 312, then minus 3 is 309. So hw is 309.\n\npm = hw + 91. hw is 309. 309 + 90 is 399, plus 1 is 400. Wait, that can't be right. Wait, 309 + 91. Let's check again. 309 + 91: 300 + 90 is 390, 9 + 1 is 10, so 390 + 10 is 400. Yes, pm is 400.\n\nnr = pm - 39. pm is 400. 400 - 30 is 370, minus 9 is 361. So nr is 361.\n\nuv = nr + 36. nr is 361. 361 + 36. 300 + 30 is 330, 60 + 6 is 66, 1 + 0 is 1. Wait, maybe better to add step by step. 361 + 30 is 391, then +6 is 397. So uv is 397.\n\nlk = uv - 34. uv is 397. 397 - 30 is 367, minus 4 is 363. So lk is 363.\n\nxa = lk + 27. lk is 363. 363 + 20 is 383, +7 is 390. So xa is 390.\n\nfv = xa - 23. xa is 390. 390 - 20 is 370, minus 3 is 367. So fv is 367.\n\nxl = fv - 10. fv is 367. 367 - 10 is 357. So xl is 357.\n\nkh = xl - 71. xl is 357. 357 - 70 is 287, minus 1 is 286. So kh is 286.\n\neg = kh + 76. kh is 286. 286 + 70 is 356, +6 is 362. So eg is 362.\n\nkg = eg - 74. eg is 362. 362 - 70 is 292, minus 4 is 288. So kg is 288.\n\nqf = kg - 57. kg is 288. 288 - 50 is 238, minus 7 is 231. So qf is 231.\n\nmx = qf - 79. qf is 231. 231 - 70 is 161, minus 9 is 152. So mx is 152.\n\nko = mx + 10. mx is 152. 152 + 10 is 162. So ko is 162.\n\nmv = ko + 21. ko is 162. 162 + 20 is 182, +1 is 183. So mv is 183.\n\nmg = mv + 69. mv is 183. 183 + 60 is 243, +9 is 252. So mg is 252.\n\nax = mg - 67. mg is 252. 252 - 60 is 192, minus 7 is 185. So ax is 185.\n\nwk = ax + 96. ax is 185. 185 + 90 is 275, +6 is 281. So wk is 281.\n\nyi = wk - 26. wk is 281. 281 - 20 is 261, minus 6 is 255. So yi is 255.\n\nhy = yi - 46. yi is 255. 255 - 40 is 215, minus 6 is 209. So hy is 209.\n\ncu = hy - 61. hy is 209. 209 - 60 is 149, minus 1 is 148. So cu is 148.\n\nhz = cu - 31. cu is 148. 148 - 30 is 118, minus 1 is 117. So hz is 117.\n\nem = hz - 66. hz is 117. 117 - 60 is 57, minus 6 is 51. So em is 51.\n\nvj = em - 49. em is 51. 51 - 40 is 11, minus 9 is 2. Wait, 51 - 49 is 2. So vj is 2.\n\nry = vj + 19. vj is 2. 2 + 19 is 21. So ry is 21.\n\nph = ry + 49. ry is 21. 21 + 40 is 61, +9 is 70. So ph is 70.\n\ncx = ph - 22. ph is 70. 70 - 20 is 50, minus 2 is 48. So cx is 48.\n\ndw = cx - 18. cx is 48. 48 - 10 is 38, minus 8 is 30. So dw is 30.\n\nWait, let me double-check some steps where I might have made a mistake. Starting from the beginning:\n\nbs = 524\n\num = 524 +22 =546 \u2714\ufe0f\n\net =546-60=486 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nud=486-94=392 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nhw=392-83=309 \u2714\ufe0f\n\npm=309+91=400 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nnr=400-39=361 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nuv=361+36=397 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nlk=397-34=363 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nxa=363+27=390 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nfv=390-23=367 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nxl=367-10=357 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nkh=357-71=286 \u2714\ufe0f\n\neg=286+76=362 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nkg=362-74=288 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nqf=288-57=231 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nmx=231-79=152 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nko=152+10=162 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nmv=162+21=183 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nmg=183+69=252 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nax=252-67=185 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nwk=185+96=281 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nyi=281-26=255 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nhy=255-46=209 \u2714\ufe0f\n\ncu=209-61=148 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nhz=148-31=117 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nem=117-66=51 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nvj=51-49=2 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nry=2+19=21 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nph=21+49=70 \u2714\ufe0f\n\ncx=70-22=48 \u2714\ufe0f\n\ndw=48-18=30 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nAll steps check out. Each calculation seems correct. So the final value of dw is 30.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe value of dw is \\boxed{30}.\n\n\n\nStarting with the given assignments, we calculate each variable step by step:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nbs &= 524, \\\\\num &= bs + 22 = 524 + 22 = 546, \\\\\net &= um - 60 = 546 - 60 = 486, \\\\\nud &= et - 94 = 486 - 94 = 392, \\\\\nhw &= ud - 83 = 392 - 83 = 309, \\\\\npm &= hw + 91 = 309 + 91 = 400, \\\\\nnr &= pm - 39 = 400 - 39 = 361, \\\\\nuv &= nr + 36 = 361 + 36 = 397, \\\\\nlk &= uv - 34 = 397 - 34 = 363, \\\\\nxa &= lk + 27 = 363 + 27 = 390, \\\\\nfv &= xa - 23 = 390 - 23 = 367, \\\\\nxl &= fv - 10 = 367 - 10 = 357, \\\\\nkh &= xl - 71 = 357 - 71 = 286, \\\\\neg &= kh + 76 = 286 + 76 = 362, \\\\\nkg &= eg - 74 = 362 - 74 = 288, \\\\\nqf &= kg - 57 = 288 - 57 = 231, \\\\\nmx &= qf - 79 = 231 - 79 = 152, \\\\\nko &= mx + 10 = 152 + 10 = 162, \\\\\nmv &= ko + 21 = 162 + 21 = 183, \\\\\nmg &= mv + 69 = 183 + 69 = 252, \\\\\nax &= mg - 67 = 252 - 67 = 185, \\\\\nwk &= ax + 96 = 185 + 96 = 281, \\\\\nyi &= wk - 26 = 281 - 26 = 255, \\\\\nhy &= yi - 46 = 255 - 46 = 209, \\\\\ncu &= hy - 61 = 209 - 61 = 148, \\\\\nhz &= cu - 31 = 148 - 31 = 117, \\\\\nem &= hz - 66 = 117 - 66 = 51, \\\\\nvj &= em - 49 = 51 - 49 = 2, \\\\\nry &= vj + 19 = 2 + 19 = 21, \\\\\nph &= ry + 49 = 21 + 49 = 70, \\\\\ncx &= ph - 22 = 70 - 22 = 48, \\\\\ndw &= cx - 18 = 48 - 18 = 30.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThe value of \\( dw \\) is \\(\\boxed{30}\\)."}
