st of variables each defined in terms of the previous ones. Starting from pe = 211, and each subsequent variable is calculated by adding or subtracting some number from the previous variable. So, I guess I need to go step by step through each assignment, compute each variable's value, and keep track until I get to \"th\". Let's start writing down each step.\n\nFirst, pe = 211. Then qo is pe minus 80. So qo = 211 - 80. Let me compute that: 211 - 80 is 131. So qo = 131.\n\nNext, bp = qo - 25. So 131 - 25 is 106. bp = 106.\n\nThen kf = bp - 79. 106 - 79 is 27. So kf = 27.\n\nud = kf + 87. 27 + 87 = 114. ud = 114.\n\ntd = ud - 66. 114 - 66 = 48. td = 48.\n\npy = td + 86. 48 + 86 = 134. py = 134.\n\nly = py - 50. 134 - 50 = 84. ly = 84.\n\nsu = ly + 47. 84 + 47 = 131. su = 131.\n\noc = su + 34. 131 + 34 = 165. oc = 165.\n\nwz = oc + 14. 165 + 14 = 179. wz = 179.\n\nip = wz - 70. 179 - 70 = 109. ip = 109.\n\ntw = ip + 21. 109 + 21 = 130. tw = 130.\n\nfm = tw + 29. 130 + 29 = 159. fm = 159.\n\nlc = fm + 20. 159 + 20 = 179. lc = 179.\n\nfn = lc - 77. 179 - 77 = 102. fn = 102.\n\ndt = fn - 76. 102 - 76 = 26. dt = 26.\n\nyj = dt + 37. 26 + 37 = 63. yj = 63.\n\njw = yj - 84. 63 - 84. Hmm, that's negative. 63 - 84 = -21. jw = -21.\n\nuz = jw - 67. So -21 - 67 = -88. uz = -88.\n\nxs = uz - 94. -88 - 94 = -182. xs = -182.\n\nfu = xs - 20. -182 - 20 = -202. fu = -202.\n\nmf = fu - 88. -202 - 88 = -290. mf = -290.\n\ndx = mf + 72. -290 + 72 = -218. dx = -218.\n\ncx = dx - 34. -218 - 34 = -252. cx = -252.\n\nna = cx + 12. -252 + 12 = -240. na = -240.\n\nsp = na - 24. -240 - 24 = -264. sp = -264.\n\nwb = sp + 57. -264 + 57. Let's calculate that. 264 - 57 is 207, so since sp is negative, it's -207. Wait, no: -264 + 57 is like subtracting 57 from 264 but since one is negative, it's -(264 - 57) + 0? Wait, maybe better to compute as (-264) + 57. 57 - 264 = -207. So wb = -207.\n\ndz = wb + 52. -207 + 52 = -155. dz = -155.\n\nny = dz - 17. -155 - 17 = -172. ny = -172.\n\nrc = ny + 28. -172