ach one depending on the previous. Maybe the best way is to go step by step, calculating each variable in order. Let me start from the beginning.\n\nFirst, wn is given as 173. Then bh is wn + 29. So bh = 173 + 29. Let me add those. 173 + 20 is 193, plus 9 is 202. So bh is 202.\n\nNext, qx = bh - 82. So 202 - 80 is 122, minus 2 more is 120. So qx is 120.\n\nThen ta = qx - 86. That's 120 - 86. Let me subtract 80 from 120, which is 40, then subtract 6 more to get 34. So ta is 34.\n\nwt = ta + 24. 34 + 24. 30 + 20 is 50, 4 + 4 is 8, so total 58. So wt is 58.\n\nap = wt + 66. 58 + 60 is 118, plus 6 is 124. So ap is 124.\n\nid = ap + 34. 124 + 30 is 154, plus 4 is 158. So id is 158.\n\nsf = id - 65. 158 - 60 is 98, minus 5 more is 93. So sf is 93.\n\ntj = sf - 67. 93 - 60 is 33, minus 7 more is 26. So tj is 26.\n\nky = tj + 97. 26 + 97. 20 + 90 is 110, 6 + 7 is 13, so 110 +13 = 123. So ky is 123.\n\nzt = ky - 28. 123 - 20 is 103, minus 8 is 95. So zt is 95.\n\ngi = zt + 25. 95 + 20 is 115, plus 5 is 120. So gi is 120.\n\nbj = gi - 68. 120 - 60 is 60, minus 8 is 52. So bj is 52.\n\nun = bj - 31. 52 - 30 is 22, minus 1 is 21. So un is 21.\n\nth = un + 32. 21 + 30 is 51, plus 2 is 53. So th is 53.\n\nmx = th - 54. Wait, 53 - 54. That would be negative. 53 minus 54 is -1. So mx is -1.\n\ncz = mx - 65. So -1 - 65 is -66. So cz is -66.\n\njv = cz + 10. -66 + 10 is -56. So jv is -56.\n\nof = jv + 52. -56 + 52. That's like subtracting 56 -52 = 4, so negative. So -4. So of is -4.\n\nbt = of - 41. -4 - 41 is -45. So bt is -45.\n\nqo = bt + 43. -45 + 43 is -2. So qo is -2.\n\nfm = qo - 61. -2 - 61 is -63. So fm is -63.\n\nxt = fm + 59. -63 + 59. That's like 59 - 63 = -4. So xt is -4.\n\nnz = xt - 96. -4 - 96 is -100. So nz is -100.\n\npa = nz + 77. -100 +77. That's like subtracting 100 -77 = 23, so -23. So pa is -23.\n\nqp = pa -76. -23 -76 = -99. So qp is -99.\n\nle = qp -87. -99 -87. That's -(99+87). Let's add 99+80=179, plus7=186. So le is -186.\n\nki = le -18. -186 -18 = -204. S