9], [6543, 6547], [6857, 6861], [6873, 6877]], "ambiguous": false}], "externalization_fraction": 1.0, "n_clean": 63}, "trace": "Okay, let's see. I need to find the value of \"ut\" based on all these assignments. There are a lot of variables here, each defined in terms of the previous ones. Starting from \"fn = 543\" and then each subsequent variable is calculated by adding or subtracting some number from the previous variable. Since all these variables are dependent on each other in a chain, I think the easiest way is to just follow the chain step by step, calculating each variable one after another. Let me write them down in order and compute each value as I go along.\n\nStarting with fn = 543.\n\nThen jo = fn - 21. So 543 - 21 = 522. So jo is 522.\n\nNext is ay = jo + 66. That would be 522 + 66. Let me add that: 522 + 60 is 582, plus 6 is 588. So ay is 588.\n\nThen yd = ay - 22. 588 - 22. Subtract 20 first: 568, then subtract 2 more: 566. So yd is 566.\n\nrp = yd - 61. 566 - 61. Let's subtract 60 first: 506, then subtract 1 more: 505. So rp is 505.\n\nhg = rp + 35. 505 + 35. 500 + 30 is 530, then 5 + 5 is 10, so total 540. Wait, 505 + 35: 500 + 30 = 530, 5 + 5 = 10, so 530 +10=540? Wait, no, 505 + 35. 505 + 30 is 535, then +5 is 540. Yes, so hg is 540.\n\net = hg + 61. 540 + 61. 540 + 60 is 600, then +1 is 601. So et is 601.\n\nzr = et + 22. 601 + 22 is 623. So zr is 623.\n\nnp = zr - 34. 623 - 34. Let's do 623 - 30 = 593, then -4 more is 589. So np is 589.\n\ndd = np + 13. 589 +13. 589 +10 is 599, +3 is 602. So dd is 602.\n\njd = dd -54. 602 -54. Let's subtract 50 first: 552, then -4 more is 548. So jd is 548.\n\nkp = jd +52. 548 +52. 500 +50 is 550, 48 +2 is 50, so 550 +50 = 600. So kp is 600.\n\nby = kp -90. 600 -90 = 510. So by is 510.\n\nmp = by +66. 510 +66. 510 +60 is 570, +6 is 576. So mp is 576.\n\nxr = mp +18. 576 +18. 576 +10=586, +8=594. So xr is 594.\n\nhb = xr +92. 594 +92. Let's add 90 first: 594 +90=684, then +2=686. So hb is 686.\n\nvt = hb +93. 686 +93. 686 +90=776, then +3=779. So vt is 779.\n\nqy = vt +16. 779 +16=795. So qy is 795.\n\nbx = qy +62. 795 +62. 700 +60=760, 95 +2=97, so 760 +97=857. So bx is 857.\n\nws = bx +28. 857 +28. 800 +20=820, 57 +8=65, so 820 +65=885. So ws is 885.\n\nav = ws -15. 885 -15=870. So av is 870.\n\nxf = av +73. 870 +73. 800 +70=870, 70 +3=73, so 870 +73=943. Wait, no: 870 +70=940, +3=943. So xf is 943.\n\nkk = xf +84. 943 +84. 900 +80=980, 43 +4=47, so 980 +47=1027. So kk is 1027.\n\nmg = kk -97. 1027 -97. Let's subtract 100 first: 927, then add back 3: 927 +3=930. So mg is 930.\n\nqp = mg -70. 930 -70=860. So qp is 860.\n\nhm = qp +92. 860 +92. 800 +90=890, 60 +2=62, so 890 +62=952. So hm is 952.\n\nhc = hm -24. 952 -24. 952 -20=932, -4=928. So hc is 928.\n\nek = hc -25. 928 -25=903. So ek is 903.\n\nwy = ek +33. 903 +33. 900 +30=930, 3 +3=6, so 930 +6=936. So wy is 936.\n\nux = wy -91. 936 -91. Subtract 90 first: 846, then subtract 1 more: 845. So ux is 845.\n\nwh = ux +53. 845 +53. 800 +50=850, 45 +3=48, so 850 +48=898. So wh is 898.\n\nck = wh +31. 898 +31. 800 +30=830, 98 +1=99, so 830 +99=929. Wait, no: 898 +31. 898 +30=928, +1=929. Yes, ck is 929.\n\nmw = ck -99. 929 -99. Subtract 100: 829, then add back 1: 830. Wait, 929 -99. 929 -100=829, but since it's 99, which is 1 less than 100, so 829 +1=830. So mw is 830.\n\nne = mw -32. 830 -32. 830 -30=800, -2=798. So ne is 798.\n\nke = ne +19. 798 +19. 798 +20=818, -1=817. So ke is 817.\n\npm = ke +55. 817 +55. 800 +50=850, 17 +5=22, so 850 +22=872. So pm is 872.\n\nmh = pm +37. 872 +37. 800 +30=830, 72 +7=79, so 830 +79=909. So mh is 909.\n\nzq = mh -72. 909 -72. 900 -70=830, 9 -2=7, so 830 +7=837. Wait, no: 909 -70=839, then -2=837. Yes, zq is 837.\n\nuh = zq +33. 837 +33. 800 +30=830, 37 +3=40, so 830 +40=870. So uh is 870.\n\nfp = uh +45. 870 +45. 800 +40=840, 70 +5=75, so 840 +75=915. So fp is 915.\n\nla = fp +84. 915 +84. 900 +80=980, 15 +4=19, so 980 +19=999. So la is 999.\n\nkr = la -89. 999 -89. 999 -90=909, +1=910. Wait, 999 -89. Subtract 80: 919, then subtract 9 more: 910. Yes, kr is 910.\n\nhh = kr +61. 910 +61. 900 +60=960, 10 +1=11, so 960 +11=971. So hh is 971.\n\nra = hh -25. 971 -25=946. So ra is 946.\n\nnm = ra +14. 946 +14=960. So nm is 960.\n\nuy = nm +58. 960 +58. 900 +50=950, 60 +8=68, so 950 +68=1018. So uy is 1018.\n\nbh = uy +36. 1018 +36. 1000 +30=1030, 18 +6=24, so 1030 +24=1054. So bh is 1054.\n\nqn = bh +72. 1054 +72. 1000 +70=1070, 54 +2=56, so 1070 +56=1126. So qn is 1126.\n\njx = qn -16. 1126 -16=1110. So jx is 1110.\n\nty = jx -69. 1110 -69. 1110 -70=1040, +1=1041. So ty is 1041.\n\nlf = ty -41. 1041 -41=1000. So lf is 1000.\n\nuj = lf +24. 1000 +24=1024. So uj is 1024.\n\nqd = uj -18. 1024 -18=1006. So qd is 1006.\n\npq = qd +32. 1006 +32=1038. So pq is 1038.\n\nmc = pq -17. 1038 -17=1021. So mc is 1021.\n\nwe = mc +73. 1021 +73. 1000 +70=1070, 21 +3=24, so 1070 +24=1094. So we is 1094.\n\nos = we +87. 1094 +87. 1000 +80=1080, 94 +7=101, so 1080 +101=1181. Wait, that doesn't seem right. Wait, 1094 +80=1174, then +7=1181. Yes, os is 1181.\n\naz = os -15. 1181 -15=1166. So az is 1166.\n\nls = az -99. 1166 -99. 1166 -100=1066, +1=1067. So ls is 1067.\n\nwr = ls +45. 1067 +45. 1000 +40=1040, 67 +5=72, so 1040 +72=1112. So wr is 1112.\n\nxl = wr +37. 1112 +37. 1100 +30=1130, 12 +7=19, so 1130 +19=1149. So xl is 1149.\n\nwc = xl -94. 1149 -94. 1100 -90=1010, 49 -4=45, so 1010 +45=1055. Wait, no: 1149 -94. Let me subtract 100 first: 1049, then add back 6: 1049 +6=1055. Yes, wc is 1055.\n\nvk = wc +66. 1055 +66. 1000 +60=1060, 55 +6=61, so 1060 +61=1121. So vk is 1121.\n\nut = vk -27. 1121 -27=1094. So ut is 1094.\n\nWait, let me double-check that last step. 1121 minus 27. 1121 -20=1101, then -7=1094. Yes, that's correct.\n\nI think I followed all the steps correctly. Let me just verify a few intermediate steps to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors. For example, when I calculated ke = ne +19 where ne was 798, that's 798 +19=817. Correct. Then pm=ke+55=817+55=872. Correct. Then mh=pm+37=872+37=909. Correct. Then zq=mh-72=909-72=837. Yes. uh=837+33=870. Correct. fp=870+45=915. Correct. la=915+84=999. Correct. kr=999-89=910. Correct. hh=910+61=971. Correct. ra=971-25=946. Correct. nm=946+14=960. Correct. uy=960+58=1018. Correct. bh=1018+36=1054. Correct. qn=1054+72=1126. Correct. jx=1126-16=1110. Correct. ty=1110-69=1041. Correct. lf=1041-41=1000. Correct. uj=1000+24=1024. Correct. qd=1024-18=1006. Correct. pq=1006+32=1038. Correct. mc=1038-17=1021. Correct. we=1021+73=1094. Correct. os=1094+87=1181. Correct. az=1181-15=1166. Correct. ls=1166-99=1067. Correct. wr=1067+45=1112. Correct. xl=1112+37=1149. Correct. wc=1149-94=1055. Correct. vk=1055+66=1121. Correct. ut=1121-27=1094. Yep, all those steps check out. So the final answer should be 1094.\n\n\n\nThe value of **ut** is calculated by following each assignment step-by-step:\n\n1. Start with **fn = 543**.\n2. Compute each subsequent variable sequentially by applying the given arithmetic operations.\n\nAfter performing all calculations through the chain of variables, the final value of **ut** is:\n\n**ut = 1094**\n\n$\\boxed{1094}$"}
